"Qwen Code Weekly: Token Costs at a Glance, Voice Input, Save & Reuse Workflows | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/en/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-06-25/)\nciteturn29779search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Transcription has two paths: batch mode (`qwen3-asr-flash`) uses OpenAI-compatible chat/completions + input_audio API; realtime mode (`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`) streams PCM via WebSocket with partial text displayed live.\n\nUI slimmed down across the board. Terminal tool-call boxes stacked into a wall of rounded borders, thinking blocks had no dedicated expand key, and extension / MCP server management required editing config files by hand. This week: borders gone, completed tools collapse to one line, Alt+T specifically manages thinking, `/extensions` becomes an interactive manager, and MCP Resources can be browsed and `@`-completed.\n\n### Voice Input: Just Talk Into Your Microphone\n\nEvery input used to be typed. Long commands, complex parameters, mixed Chinese-English — slow and easy to mistype.\n\nThis week adds `/voice` voice input. Two modes: hold mode — press Space to talk, release to stop; tap mode — click once to start, click again or silence auto-stops and submits. Audio is captured via a native microphone backend (`@qwen-code/audio-capture` N-API addon). On Linux it auto-falls back to arecord/SoX; on macOS it requests microphone permission.\n\nTranscription has two paths: batch mode (`qwen3-asr-flash`) uses OpenAI-compatible chat/completions + input_audio API; realtime mode (`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`) streams PCM via WebSocket with partial text displayed live. After you finish, the fast model cleans up filler words (“um”, “嗯”) and typos while preserving your original phrasing — no rewriting. On timeout or failure, the raw transcript is used directly. Voice input always produces text.\n\n`/model --voice` selects the transcription model; `general.voice.{enabled,mode,language}` configures behavior.\n\nWhat you can do with it:\n\n  * `/voice hold` — hold Space to talk, release to stop transcription\n  * `/voice tap` — click once to start, speak a sentence or silence to stop\n  * `/model --voice qwen3-asr-flash-realtime` — pick a realtime streaming transcription model\n  * `/voice status` — check current voice configuration\n  * Web Shell: click the microphone button for voice input (browser recording, daemon-side transcription)\n\nSee PR #5502 , #5794 , #5755 \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVision & audio APIs cookbook — Qwen MM Plugins (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-mm-plugins-hub/plugins/api/cookbook/)\nciteturn29779search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago;   * `transcribe_audio` — transcribe audio/video with `qwen3-asr-flash` or `ASR_SERVER_URLS`; returns SRT, text, or JSON.\n## Tools\n\n### Vision\n\n  * `vision_chat` — ask questions about images or videos using `images`, `videos`, and `text`.\n  * `ocr` — extract text from a local image.\n  * `grounding` — locate objects and return pixel and normalized boxes. Pass `bbox_normalized` to core's `draw_bbox` for annotation.\n\n### Omni\n\nTool  | Use\n--- | ---\n`omni_asr`  | Speech transcription\n`omni_asr_timestamped`  | Timestamped transcripts and SRT subtitles\n`omni_multi_speaker_asr`  | Speaker-labelled transcripts\n`omni_av_caption`  | Audio/video descriptions, visible text, and dialogue\n`omni_av_grounding`  | Find an event's start and end times\n`omni_av_counting`  | Count events or actions with timestamps\n`omni_music_caption`  | Music descriptions and structured tags\n\nOmni tools accept a local audio/video `file_path` or an HTTP(S)/OSS URL. Use `fps` and `max_pixels` to control video sampling where the tool exposes them.\n\n### Other services\n\n  * `transcribe_audio` — transcribe audio/video with `qwen3-asr-flash` or `ASR_SERVER_URLS`; returns SRT, text, or JSON.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code 周报：/loop 自主模式、桌面端语音听写、Settings 标签式视图 | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/zh/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-07-02/)\nciteturn29779search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; 转写在服务端进行，复用 CLI 的语音管线（批量 `qwen3-asr-flash` 与实时 `*-realtime` 模型），provider 凭证不会进入 renderer。 ...   * 选择 realtime 模型（如 `qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`）边说边看 interim 文本\n### 桌面端语音听写：三端能力对齐\n\n语音听写在 CLI 和 Web Shell 里已经有了，但桌面端缺失——用户配置好语音后一切到桌面端就失去这个能力。本版本补齐了最后一个界面。\n\ncomposer 工具栏新增麦克风按钮，录音时工具栏变成录音条（点线引导 → 实时波形 → 计时），停止后转写结果插入输入框供复核。转写在服务端进行，复用 CLI 的语音管线（批量 `qwen3-asr-flash` 与实时 `*-realtime` 模型），provider 凭证不会进入 renderer。语音可在 Settings → Input 和 composer 模型下拉里开关并选择模型。\n\n你能用它做什么：\n\n  * 点击麦克风说话，实时看到波形和计时\n  * 选择 realtime 模型（如 `qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`）边说边看 interim 文本\n  * 在平板或多显示器场景下解放双手输入\n\n详见 PR #5856 \n\n> 如何使用？\n> \n>   1. 克隆仓库：\n>     \n>     `git clone https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code.git`\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code 周报：Token 花了多少一目了然、语音输入不用手打、工作流可保存复用 | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/zh/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-06-25/)\nciteturn29779search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; 转录有两条路径：batch 模式（`qwen3-asr-flash`）用 OpenAI-compatible chat/completions + input_audio API；realtime 模式（`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`、`fun-asr-realtime`）通过 WebSocket 流式 PCM，屏幕上实时显示部分转录文字。\n这周边框去掉、已完成工具折叠成一行、Alt+T 专门管 thinking、`/extensions` 变成交互式管理器、MCP Resources 能浏览和 `@` 补全。\n\n### 语音输入：对着麦克风说话就行\n\n之前所有输入都是手打的。长命令、复杂参数、中英混排，打字慢还容易拼错。\n\n这周新增 `/voice` 语音输入。两种模式：hold 模式按住 Space 说话，松手停止；tap 模式点一下开始，再点一下或静音自动停止提交。音频通过原生麦克风后端捕获（`@qwen-code/audio-capture` N-API addon），Linux 上自动 fallback 到 arecord/SoX，macOS 自动请求麦克风权限。\n\n转录有两条路径：batch 模式（`qwen3-asr-flash`）用 OpenAI-compatible chat/completions + input_audio API；realtime 模式（`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`、`fun-asr-realtime`）通过 WebSocket 流式 PCM，屏幕上实时显示部分转录文字。说完后 fast model 自动清理语气词（“um”、” 嗯 “）和错别字，保留原始表达不做改写——超时或失败时直接用原始转录文本，语音输入永远产出文字。\n\n`/model --voice` 选择转录模型，`general.voice.{enabled,mode,language}` 配置行为。\n\n你能用它做什么：\n\n  * `/voice hold` 按住 Space 说话，松手停止转录\n  * `/voice tap` 点一下开始，再说一句或静音停止\n  * `/model --voice qwen3-asr-flash-realtime` 选实时流式转录模型\n  * `/voice status` 查看当前语音配置\n  * Web Shell 点击麦克风按钮也能语音输入（浏览器录音，daemon 端转录）\n\n详见 PR #5502 、#5794 、#5755 \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code Hebdo : Coût des tokens en un coup d'œil, saisie vocale, workflows réutilisables | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/fr/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-06-25/)\nciteturn29779search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; La transcription a deux chemins : mode batch (`qwen3-asr-flash`) utilise l’API chat/completions compatible OpenAI + input_audio ; mode temps réel (`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`) diffuse PCM via WebSocket avec affichage partiel en direct.\nL’audio est capturé via un backend natif de microphone (`@qwen-code/audio-capture` addon N-API). Sur Linux, il bascule automatiquement vers arecord/SoX ; sur macOS, il demande la permission du microphone.\n\nLa transcription a deux chemins : mode batch (`qwen3-asr-flash`) utilise l’API chat/completions compatible OpenAI + input_audio ; mode temps réel (`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`) diffuse PCM via WebSocket avec affichage partiel en direct. Une fois terminé, le modèle rapide nettoie les mots de remplissage (« um », « 嗯 ») et les fautes tout en préservant votre formulation originale — pas de réécriture. En cas de timeout ou d’échec, la transcription brute est utilisée directement. La saisie vocale produit toujours du texte.\n\n`/model --voice` sélectionne le modèle de transcription ; `general.voice.{enabled,mode,language}` configure le comportement.\n\nCe que vous pouvez faire avec :\n\n  * `/voice hold` — maintenez Espace pour parler, relâchez pour arrêter la transcription\n  * `/voice tap` — cliquez une fois pour démarrer, parlez une phrase ou le silence arrête\n  * `/model --voice qwen3-asr-flash-realtime` — choisissez un modèle de transcription en streaming temps réel\n  * `/voice status` — vérifiez la configuration vocale actuelle\n  * Web Shell : cliquez sur le bouton microphone pour la saisie vocale (enregistrement navigateur, transcription côté daemon)\n\nVoir PR #5502 , #5794 , #5755 \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code Hebdo : Mode autonome /loop, dictée vocale sur Desktop, vue par onglets des Settings | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/fr/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-07-02/)\nciteturn29779search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; La transcription s’effectue côté serveur, réutilisant le pipeline vocal du CLI (batch `qwen3-asr-flash` et modèles temps réel `*-realtime`) — les credentials du provider n’entrent jamais dans le renderer.\n  * Choisissez un modèle temps réel (comme `qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`) pour voir le texte provisoire pendant que vous parlez\n  * Gardez les mains libres pour la saisie sur tablette ou dans des configurations multi-écrans\n\nVoir PR #5856 \n\n> Comment utiliser ?\n> \n>   1. Clonez le dépôt :\n>     \n>     `git clone https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code.git`\n> \n>   2. Accédez au répertoire\n>     \n>     `cd qwen-code/packages/desktop`\n> \n>   3. Installez les dépendances et lancez le mode développement\n>     \n>     `bun install && bun run dev`\n\n### Mobile Sidebar Drawer + finalisation de l’expérience `qwen serve`\n\nAuparavant, lors de l’accès à `qwen serve` depuis un navigateur mobile, la barre latérale (liste des sessions, recherche, nouvelle session) était masquée via `display: none` en dessous de 760px — il n’y avait aucun moyen de changer de session. Un mode overlay drawer remplace désormais le masquage : un bouton menu apparaît dans l’en-tête du panneau de chat, et la barre latérale glisse depuis la gauche avec un fond semi-transparent. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code Weekly: /loop Autonomer Modus, Desktop-Spracheingabe, Settings-Tab-Ansicht | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/de/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-07-02/)\nciteturn29779search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; Die Transkription läuft serverseitig und nutzt die bestehende CLI-Sprach-Pipeline (Batch `qwen3-asr-flash` und Realtime `*-realtime` Modelle) — Provider-Credentials gelangen nicht in den Renderer.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code Еженедельно: Автономный режим /loop, голосовой ввод на десктопе, вкладочный вид Settings | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/ru/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-07-02/)\nciteturn29779search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; Транскрипция выполняется на стороне сервера, повторно используя голосовой конвейер CLI (пакетный `qwen3-asr-flash` и потоковый `*-realtime` модели), учетные данные provider не попадают в renderer.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code 주간 업데이트: /loop 자율 모드, 데스크톱 앱 음성 받아쓰기, Settings 탭형 뷰 | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/ko/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-07-02/)\nciteturn29779search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; 전사는 서버에서 수행되며 CLI의 음성 파이프라인을 그대로 재사용합니다(일괄 `qwen3-asr-flash`와 실시간 `*-realtime` 모델).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code 주간 업데이트: token 사용량 한눈에, 음성 입력으로 타이핑 생략, 워크플로 저장 후 재사용 | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/ko/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-06-25/)\nciteturn29779search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; 전사에는 두 경로가 있습니다. batch 모드(`qwen3-asr-flash`)는 OpenAI 호환 chat/completions + input_audio API를 쓰고, realtime 모드(`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`)는 WebSocket으로 PCM을 스트리밍하면서 화면에 부분 전사 텍스트를 실시간 표시합니다.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code Semanal: Custo de Tokens em um Olhar, Entrada por Voz, Workflows Salvos e Reutilizáveis | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/pt-BR/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-06-25/)\nciteturn29779search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Transcrição tem dois caminhos: modo batch (`qwen3-asr-flash`) usa API chat/completions compatível com OpenAI + input_audio; modo tempo real (`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`) transmite PCM via WebSocket com exibição parcial ao vivo.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen Code Еженедельно: Стоимость токенов на виду, голосовой ввод, сохранение и повторное использование рабочих процессов | Qwen Code Docs (https://qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs/ru/blog/updates/weekly-update-2026-06-25/)\nciteturn29779search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Транскрипция имеет два пути: пакетный режим (`qwen3-asr-flash`) использует API chat/completions совместимый с OpenAI + input_audio; режим реального времени (`qwen3-asr-flash-realtime`, `fun-asr-realtime`) передает PCM через WebSocket с отображением частичного текста в реальном времени.\n"
